        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(browser): apply profile proxy policy to tab list redaction",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n`/tabs` and `/tabs/action` list redaction only used the global SSRF policy. They did not include the selected profile's browser proxy mode, while tab open/focus/select already use `browserNavigationPolicyForProfile`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\nStrict browser navigation policy depends on whether the browser profile itself is proxy-routed. Tab list URL redaction is a navigation-result policy check, so it should receive the same profile-aware policy as the other tab routes.\n\n## User Impact\nTab list responses now redact URLs consistently for proxy-routed browser profiles instead of evaluating them with an incomplete policy. This keeps list responses aligned with focus/select safety checks.\n\n## Evidence\n- Changed tab list redaction to accept `browserNavigationPolicyForProfile(ctx, profileCtx)`.\n- Added route regression coverage for both `/tabs` and `/tabs/action list` passing `explicit-browser-proxy` into result guards.\n- Added attach-only route proof in `extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.attach-only.test.ts` that uses the real browser route context and real navigation guard: strict SSRF plus `--proxy-server=...` redacts a public IP-literal tab URL for both list endpoints.\n- Focused tests:\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.attach-only.test.ts -- --reporter=verbose`\n  - Result: 2 files / 24 tests passed.\n- Touched-file checks:\n  - `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.attach-only.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.test.ts`\n  - `OPENCLAW_OXLINT_SKIP_PREPARE=1 node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.attach-only.test.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.ts extensions/browser/src/browser/routes/tabs.test.ts`\n  - `git diff --check`\n- Autoreview closeout:\n  - `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine claude --prompt '<scope prompt>'`\n  - Result: clean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n\n## Proof\nThe original route regression verifies the policy object passed to the redaction guard. The attach-only regression now exercises the same route handlers with the real navigation guard and a loopback OpenClaw CDP profile configured with `--proxy-server=...`; under strict SSRF, the tab list response keeps the tab identity but blanks the URL for both `GET /tabs` and `POST /tabs/action { action: \"list\" }`. This proof does not require a live proxy or credentials because the changed behavior is the preflight navigation-result policy decision before any browser network request.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/browser-tabs-profile-proxy-redaction-20260711",
